    "turn_text": "So this weekend, we celebrate the transition, the ascension of Mother Thelma Mother Shed wear. This is a hyphenate the last day Mother Shed dash W-A-I-R who passed away after a remarkable life of trailblazing. But she was one of the original Little Rock Central High School integrators known as the Little Rock Nine, who in 1957 integrated Little Rock Central High School on the orders of the federal government pursuant to 1954's desegregation orders in Brown versus Board of Education. We all know Ernest Green and those other students who so bravely integrated Little Rock Central in front of the screaming mobs and endured that she lived not far from my hometown of St. Louis. She lived right across the river in East St. Louis and was an active citizen church corps public school teacher for the bulk of her adult life and past this weekend in Little Rock. So just wanted to acknowledge her passing and She's 83 years old was of sound mind and such, you know, this is in our lifetimes, you know, and we look at those pictures and they're black and white and the footage is not HD so we can kind of, you know, delude ourselves into believing that that was a different time in a different era. Well, it wasn't. This is somebody who's 83 years old. Everybody listening here knows somebody who was active and engaged at 83 and this was in their lifetimes that our parents and grandparents still integrated their schools. And I think you can't disconnect that from this election coming up is like, there is one side that clearly wants to take us back to that when Trump talks about, as he said very clearly, defunding, excuse me, he didn't say defund. He said, eliminate, abolish the Department of Education. Well, that's where this takes us back to. because the Department of Education has an active civil rights department that deals with K through 12 as well as higher education. And that civil rights department is charged with making sure that federal and state resources determined for education meet out a fair education regardless of racial demographics across this country. And Trump sat there on Fox News's flagship morning broadcast and said that it's over with. He also said that we are going to not fund cities that teach history based upon accurate history, right? So, you know, as these Titans kind of passed right in front of our eyes, let them, honestly, let us honor their lives, but let them serve as a stark reminder of an era in which people survive something that we have the power to not go back to.",
